{"mutants":[{"bug":"Uses an inclusive seconds limit, allowing the seconds counter to reach 60 before rolling over.","trigger":"While running with hour=0, on a one_sec_pulse when seconds=59; for example, the 60th pulse after seconds reaches 0.","effect":"seconds becomes 60 for one second interval, then rolls to 0 on the next pulse and advances minutes.","edits":[{"old":"if (seconds < 59) begin","new":"if (seconds <= 59) begin"}]},{"bug":"Uses an inclusive minutes limit, allowing the minutes counter to reach 60 before the hour is set.","trigger":"While running with hour=0 and minutes=59, on the one_sec_pulse that rolls seconds from 59 to 0.","effect":"minutes becomes 60 and hour remains 0 until the next seconds rollover, when minutes resets and hour is set.","edits":[{"old":"if (minutes < 59) begin","new":"if (minutes <= 59) begin"}]},{"bug":"Clears the divider counter when paused instead of preserving its partial count.","trigger":"Deassert start_stop while counter is between 1 and COUNTER_MAX-1, then resume; for example, pause at counter=COUNTER_MAX/2.","effect":"The partial second is discarded, so the next one-second pulse occurs later than it would with a preserved count.","edits":[{"old":"            end else begin
                one_sec_pulse <= 1'b0;           // Ensure one_sec_pulse is cleared if paused
            end","new":"            end else begin
                counter <= 0;
                one_sec_pulse <= 1'b0;           // Ensure one_sec_pulse is cleared if paused
            end"}]},{"bug":"Removes asynchronous reset sensitivity from the stopwatch logic.","trigger":"Assert and deassert reset between one_sec_pulse rising edges, without a pulse while reset is asserted.","effect":"seconds, minutes, and hour retain their pre-reset values instead of clearing when reset is asserted.","edits":[{"old":"    always @(posedge one_sec_pulse or posedge reset) begin","new":"    always @(posedge one_sec_pulse) begin"}]},{"bug":"Omits the hour=0 guard, so the stopwatch does not stop after reaching its terminal hour state.","trigger":"Run continuously through the hour transition: 60×60 one_sec_pulse events from 00:00:00, then observe the next pulse after hour becomes 1.","effect":"The stopwatch continues advancing seconds and minutes after hour reaches 1, rather than holding its terminal time.","edits":[{"old":"end else if (start_stop == 1 && hour == 0) begin","new":"end else if (start_stop == 1) begin"}]}]}

{"mutants":[{"bug":"Divider counter is one bit too narrow for some parameter values.","trigger":"With CLK_FREQ=17, COUNTER_MAX is 16, but the replacement declaration makes counter 4 bits wide. While running, it cycles from 0 through 15 and wraps to 0, so it never reaches the terminal count.","effect":"The divider never generates a one-second pulse, and the stopwatch counters do not advance.","edits":[{"old":"reg [$clog2(COUNTER_MAX):0] counter;    // Clock divider counter width based on CLK_FREQ","new":"reg [$clog2(COUNTER_MAX)-1:0] counter;    // Clock divider counter width based on CLK_FREQ"}]},{"bug":"The divider counter is cleared whenever the stopwatch is paused instead of retaining fractional progress.","trigger":"For example, with CLK_FREQ=10, let the counter reach 4 while running, pause for a clock edge, then resume. The pause clears the nonzero counter; repeated pauses discard accumulated progress.","effect":"After a pause and resume, the next one-second pulse occurs later than it would if the divider retained its count.","edits":[{"old":"end else begin
                one_sec_pulse <= 1'b0;           // Ensure one_sec_pulse is cleared if paused
            end","new":"end else begin
